    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="70.1">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IICn">II Cn</ref> 70.1</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="70.1" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="356" ed="#liebermann"/>Ac beo be his dihte seo æht<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="17" target="#IICn_70-1.lnote.oe.17-2"/> gescyft swyðe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="19" target="#IICn_70-1.lnote.oe.19"/> rihte wife ⁊ cildu<hi rend="italic">m<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="20" target="#IICn_70-1.lnote.oe.20"/></hi> ⁊ nehmagu<hi rend="italic">m</hi>, ælcu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> be þære mæðe, þe hi<hi rend="italic">m</hi> to gebyrige.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="70.1" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="356" ed="#liebermann"/>Ac beo be his dihte seo æht gescyft swyðe rihte wife ⁊ cildan ⁊ neahmagon, ælcon be ðære mæðe, ðe him to gebyrige.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="70.1" corresp="#wit-a"><pb n="356" ed="#liebermann"/>Ac beo be his dihte seo æht gescyft swiðe rihte wife ⁊ cildan ⁊ nehmagon, ælcu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> be þære mæðe, þe him to gebyrige.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#IICn_70-1.lnote.oe.5"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="70.1" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="357" ed="#liebermann"/>Sed sit secundum dictionem<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="15" target="#IICn_70-1.lnote.oe.15"/> eius ipsa pecunia recte<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="16" target="#IICn_70-1.lnote.oe.16"/> diuisa uxori, pueris, propinquis, unicuique secundum modum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="17" target="#IICn_70-1.lnote.oe.17"/>, qui ad eum pertinet.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="70.1" corresp="#wit-inst-cn"><pb n="357" ed="#liebermann"/>Sed omnia illius diuidantur secundum ordinationem suam mulieri et<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#IICn_70-1.lnote.oe.12"/> infantibus<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#IICn_70-1.lnote.oe.13"/> et parentibus suis.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="70.1" corresp="#wit-cons-cn"><pb n="357" ed="#liebermann"/>Sed possessio intestati ipsius ex dispositione illius rectissime diuidatur uxori prolique et cognatis, cuique iuxta modum oportunum.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="70.1" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="208" ed="#robertson"/>Ac beo be his dihte seo æht gescyft swyðe rihte wife ⁊ cildan ⁊ neahmagon, ælcon be ðære mæðe ðe him to gebyrige.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="290" ed="#rabin-doml"/>Ac beo be his dihte, seo æht gescyft swyðe rihte wife and cildum and nehmagum, ælcum be þære mæðe, þe him to gebyrige.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="357" ed="#liebermann"/>Vielmehr werde unter seiner<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_70-1.lnote.de.1"/> Anordnung<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_70-1.lnote.de.2"/> die Habe höchst gerecht vertheilt<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_70-1.lnote.de.3"/> an<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#IICn_70-1.lnote.de.4"/> Ehefrau und Kinder und nahe Verwandte, jedem nach dem Maass<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#IICn_70-1.lnote.de.5"/>, das ihm gebührt.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">Rather, let the property be distributed, under his direction, most justly to wife and children and near kinsmen, to each according to the measure that is due to him.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="209" ed="#robertson"/>But, according to his direction, the property shall be very strictly divided among his wife and children and near kinsmen, each according to the share which belongs to him.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="472" ed="#whitelock"/>But by his direction, the property is to be very justly divided among the wife, the children and the close kinsmen, each in the proportion which belongs to him.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="291" ed="#rabin-doml"/>But under his direction, the estate shall be divided most fairly among his wife, children, and close relatives, each receiving the share appropriate for them.</ab>
        <note type="editorial">BR: added from Gesetze I p. 357, October 2026 (MS Cons)</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_70-1.lnote.oe.15" n="15" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">357</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">distinctionem illius <hi rend="italic">K</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">distinctionem illius K</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_70-1.lnote.oe.16" n="16" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">357</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt K</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in K</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_70-1.lnote.oe.17" n="17" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">357</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">qui ad e. p. m. <hi rend="italic">T</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">qui ad e. p. m. T</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_70-1.lnote.oe.17-2" n="17" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">356</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">æhte <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">æhte Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_70-1.lnote.oe.19" n="19" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">356</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">swiþe <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">swiþe Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_70-1.lnote.oe.20" n="20" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">356</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-dan ⁊ nehmagon, æ. be þær <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-dan ⁊ nehmagon, æ. be þær Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_70-1.lnote.oe.5" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">356</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">verbessert aus</hi> byrige</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">corrected from byrige</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_70-1.lnote.oe.12" n="12" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">357</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt Lb</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in Lb</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_70-1.lnote.oe.13" n="13" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">357</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">par. et i. <hi rend="italic">Cb</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">par. et i. Cb</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_70-1.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">211</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Der Herr muss sich jedenfalls mit Heergewäte begnügen; wo ein Testament vorliegt, muss er es gelten lassen; wo nicht, darf er den Rest nur verteilen; Maitland <hi rend="italic">Domesday</hi> 298</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">The lord must in any case be content with the heriot; where there is a will, he must let it stand; where there is none, he may only distribute the remainder; Maitland <hi rend="italic">Domesday</hi> 298</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_70-1.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">211</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">dictio</hi> (<hi rend="italic">s. Wb</hi>) wählt Q des Gleichklangs wegen</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Q chooses <hi rend="italic">dictio</hi> (<hi rend="italic">see Wb</hi>) for the sake of the assonance</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_70-1.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">211</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Lehnwort aus Nordischem</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Loan-word from Norse</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_70-1.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">211</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Keine Erbrechtsregel, nach der etwa Schwester und Bruder gleich erbten, sondern wie <hi rend="italic">u</hi>. 72, nur anderes Wort für <hi rend="italic">yrfenuman</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Not a rule of inheritance under which, say, sister and brother inherited equally, but, as <hi rend="italic">below</hi> 72, merely another word for <hi rend="italic">yrfenuman</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_70-1.lnote.de.5" n="5" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">211</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Nach Verwandtschaftsgrad</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">According to degree of kinship</seg></note>
      </div>
